      "The Lake Chad Basin has supported human settlement for thousands of years and is home to over 200 ethnic groups, including Sara peoples in the south, Barma, Kanembu, Kotoko, and Maba in the center, and Arab, Toubou (Tubu), and Daza groups in the north.",
